  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 257 AM EDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nCurrent-Fri...Strengthening high pressure encompassing much of the \neastern CONUS extending across the Deep South will help create a \ntight pressure gradient allowing for a continuation of NERLY winds. \nThis will support 10-15 mph winds with gusts to 20-25 mph today with \nwinds a little stronger into Fri. Speeds drop to 5-10 mph tonight \nand perhaps a little higher at the coast. For Fri night, winds stay \nelevated further along the coast (15 mph with higher gusts). A slug \nof moisture southward will keep rain chances confined to mostly\nSt. Lucie/Martin counties through tonight, spreading further north\nalong the coast on Fri. PoPs 20-40% along the St. Lucie/Martin \ncoasts may have to be bumped up depending on trends. Precip totals\ncould add up from repeated rounds. Highest PoPs will be located\nover the adjacent coastal waters. \n\nMax temps slightly below climo in the U70s to L80s each day. Min \ntemps mostly in the 60s with U50s well into the interior overnight \nand 60s almost everywhere Fri overnight, save for near 70F to L70s\nalong the Space/Treasure coasts. \n\nSat-Wed...Highly unsettled weather pattern as we venture into the \nweekend and early next week. Mid-upper level ridging amplifies over \nthe central CONUS as troughing engulfs the FL Straits and Bahamas. A \nsurface low pressure will develop along an old frontal boundary near \nto northeast of the Bahamas. Moisture deepens and rain chances \nincrease into the weekend-early next week. May have to be mindful\nof some heavy rainfall potential. Greatest threat along the coast\nand/or southward where moisture is deepest. The pressure gradient\ntightens further, once again, and NE/ENE winds strengthen. Expect\nwindy/gusty conditions Sat/Sun/Mon with speeds increasing 20-30 \nmph sustained this weekend and frequent higher gusts. Wind \nAdvisories may be necessary, at least for the coast. Breezy \nconditions persist into Tue, then the pgrad relaxes a bit into \nmid-week.\n\nThese strong winds will coincide with high astronomical tides and \nhelp produce another hazardous coastal event. Confidence increasing \nthat we will see beach erosion, rough surf, minor coastal flooding, \nand dangerous rip currents this weekend into early next week. Max \ntemps remain consistent near/just below seasonal norms. Above normal \novernight lows in the M60s across the interior and U60s-L70s at the \ncoast due to the strong onshore flow.",
